{"id":"e13t3","name":"Win-back Campaign List","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The CRM team prepares a win-back campaign. It targets customers who signed up before the second quarter of 2024 but did not place any real order during that quarter. For each of them, the team also wants the date of their most recent real order before the quarter.</p>\n<h3>Tables</h3>\n<p><code>customers</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>full_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(50)</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>signup_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>not null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>order_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>primary key</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n<td>NULL for guest checkouts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>order_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n<td>not null, no time part</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>status</td>\n<td>VARCHAR(20)</td>\n<td>not null, one of <code>'delivered'</code>, <code>'shipped'</code>, <code>'cancelled'</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>A real order is an order whose status is not <code>'cancelled'</code>.</li>\n<li>A customer is eligible if <code>signup_date</code> is strictly before <code>2024-04-01</code>.</li>\n<li>Return every eligible customer who has no real order with <code>order_date</code> between <code>2024-04-01</code> and <code>2024-06-30</code> (both inclusive).</li>\n<li><code>last_order_date</code> is the most recent <code>order_date</code> among the customer's real orders placed strictly before <code>2024-04-01</code>, or NULL if there is none.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>Exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>INT</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>full_name</td>\n<td>VARCHAR</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>signup_date</td>\n<td>DATE</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>last_order_date</td>\n<td>DATE (may be NULL)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>last_order_date</code> ascending with NULL values last, then <code>customer_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>customers</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>full_name</th>\n<th>signup_date</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Amina</td>\n<td>2023-11-02</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Youssef</td>\n<td>2024-01-15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Salma</td>\n<td>2024-02-20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Omar</td>\n<td>2024-03-31</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Nadia</td>\n<td>2024-04-01</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Karim</td>\n<td>2023-12-10</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>orders</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>order_id</th>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>order_date</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>101</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-01-10</td>\n<td>delivered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>102</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2024-05-03</td>\n<td>delivered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>103</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-02-01</td>\n<td>delivered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>104</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2024-04-20</td>\n<td>cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>105</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n<td>2024-03-05</td>\n<td>delivered</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>106</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>2024-07-02</td>\n<td>shipped</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>107</td>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>2024-03-31</td>\n<td>cancelled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>108</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>2024-03-15</td>\n<td>shipped</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>109</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>2024-03-28</td>\n<td>delivered</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>full_name</th>\n<th>signup_date</th>\n<th>last_order_date</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Youssef</td>\n<td>2024-01-15</td>\n<td>2024-02-01</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Karim</td>\n<td>2023-12-10</td>\n<td>2024-03-28</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Salma</td>\n<td>2024-02-20</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Omar</td>\n<td>2024-03-31</td>\n<td>NULL</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Dialect: PostgreSQL.</li>\n<li>Write a single <code>SELECT</code> statement (CTEs allowed). Do not create tables or views.</li>\n<li><code>customers</code> has up to 10^5 rows, <code>orders</code> up to 10^6 rows.</li>\n</ul><p class=\"muted\">Write a PostgreSQL query.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>customers</code>, <code>orders</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>customer_id</code>, <code>full_name</code>, <code>signup_date</code>, <code>last_order_date</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°5, question 3","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>customers</code>, <code>orders</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 4 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>customer_id</code>, <code>full_name</code>, <code>signup_date</code>, <code>last_order_date</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : ton test visible tourne.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 1/1. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 4 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"customers":{"columns":[["customer_id","INT"],["full_name","VARCHAR(50)"],["signup_date","DATE"]],"rows":[[1,"Amina","2023-11-02"],[2,"Youssef","2024-01-15"],[3,"Salma","2024-02-20"],[4,"Omar","2024-03-31"],[5,"Nadia","2024-04-01"],[6,"Karim","2023-12-10"]]},"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["order_date","DATE"],["status","VARCHAR(20)"]],"rows":[[101,1,"2024-01-10","delivered"],[102,1,"2024-05-03","delivered"],[103,2,"2024-02-01","delivered"],[104,2,"2024-04-20","cancelled"],[105,null,"2024-03-05","delivered"],[106,3,"2024-07-02","shipped"],[107,4,"2024-03-31","cancelled"],[108,6,"2024-03-15","shipped"],[109,6,"2024-03-28","delivered"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["customer_id","full_name","signup_date","last_order_date"],"rows":[[2,"Youssef","2024-01-15","2024-02-01"],[6,"Karim","2023-12-10","2024-03-28"],[3,"Salma","2024-02-20",null],[4,"Omar","2024-03-31",null]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}